This project is based on the development of digital literacy skills that are very important in the digital world that we are living in. Being a student digital ambassador, the aim of this project is to learn and apply the knowledge related to digital tools, online communication, professional platforms, and cyber safety. Digital literacy is very important in helping the student community use technology effectively in learning, communicating, and developing their careers.
The project comprises five different tasks, each based on the knowledge gained from the different modules of the course. The five tasks include creating a digital literacy awareness infographic, creating a digital portfolio, exploring coding and collaboration platforms, understanding communication etiquette, and learning about cybercrime prevention. From this project, I gained knowledge related to the different digital platforms and how to use them in the most efficient way.

Task 1: Digital Literacy Awareness Infographic
For this task, I created a digital literacy awareness infographic that helps the student community understand the importance of digital literacy. To design the infographic, I made use of the Prezi platform. The design is based on the knowledge gained from the module related to digital literacy. The infographic contains important topics such as the definition of digital literacy, digital tools that are very important for the student community, and safe internet practices. It also includes the importance of maintaining a professional online presence and the efficient use of digital platforms.
The design is based on the knowledge that the information presented must be simple and attractive enough for the student community to understand the importance of digital literacy. The final design of the infographic is exported and placed in the task-1-presentation folder in the repository.
Learning Outcome:
From this task, I learned how to creatively express myself using digital tools. This task enhanced my presentation and design skills, and I understood the need to spread awareness among students about the importance of digital literacy.

Task 2: Build Your Student Digital Portfolio
In this task, the focus is to build a professional digital identity by creating profiles on key digital platforms. For this task, I chose to create profiles on GitHub, LinkedIn, and ResearchGate.
On GitHub, I created and managed my coding profile and added a profile README containing my academic details and learning objectives. On LinkedIn, I created my professional profile and added my educational details, such as my degree and expected year of graduation. I also created a profile on ResearchGate, which is an academic platform for researchers to share content and network. These profiles are important for creating opportunities for internships and jobs. A screenshot of all the profiles has been added to the task-2-portfolio folder.
Learning Outcome:
From this task, I understood the importance of having a professional online presence. These profiles will help me showcase my skills and network, which will be beneficial for my academic and professional growth.

